1
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,780
Clash! God vs. Ryotsu

2
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:10,800
Senpai! Senpai!

3
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,540
Please wake up quickly.

4
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:16,980
We're going to be late.

5
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:25,800
Shut up.

6
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,620
Guess I'll get up now.

7
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:37,140
What is this, a bookshelf?

8
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:39,280
So noisy.

9
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:41,160
But I slept well.

10
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,000
It's just a chicken.

11
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:51,580
Isn't this just like a chicken?

12
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,360
This is my spot!

13
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:00,380
Mine!

14
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:01,500
Ryotsu!

15
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:03,040
Don't run away!

16
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:04,160
Whoa!

17
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:05,200
Whoa!

18
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:06,340
Whoa!

19
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:07,580
Whoa!

20
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:07,860
Whoa!

21
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:08,300
Whoa!

22
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:13,660
It's really a chicken.

23
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:15,140
I wonder how much it weighs per gram?

24
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:16,720
It'd make a good side dish for dinner.

25
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:17,940
Cluck!

26
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,280
This isn't a fake, you know!

27
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:22,020
Yeah.

28
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:25,000
Standing around here won't get us anywhere.

29
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,980
Let's just head to work for now.

30
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:28,140
Squawk!

31
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:33,960
Good morning.

32
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:35,000
Ryotsu!

33
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,340
What time do you think it is?

34
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:42,300
You don't have any awareness of
being a full-fledged working adult.

35
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:42,600
Chief.

36
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:46,720
Cock-a-doodle-doo?

37
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,140
Ow ow

38
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,480
What's wrong, Ryotsu?
Did you eat something bad?

39
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:58,506
I've always thought you were inhuman,

40
00:01:58,556 --> 00:02:00,400
but to actually die like a human being...

41
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,480
Could this be divine punishment?

42
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:05,740
Divine punishment?

43
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:11,720
Ryo-chan's always up to no good,
so the gods in heaven have punished him.

44
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:14,380
What bad things have I ever done?

45
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:16,100
Don't blame me!

46
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:19,920
That's right! If you have complaints,
you should take them up with the gods!

47
00:02:19,920 --> 00:02:20,400
Yeah.

48
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:23,920
Yeah, you're absolutely right.

49
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,940
I'm just going up to heaven for a bit.

50
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,440
"Going up," he says.

51
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:33,140
Do you even know where it is?

52
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:36,280
It's called heaven,
so it must be up in the sky, right?

53
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,380
Chickens can't fly, you know.

54
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:55,884
Aaaaaaaaaaaaah...

55
00:02:55,934 --> 00:02:59,504
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

56
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:03,100
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

57
00:03:03,150 --> 00:03:06,746
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

58
00:03:06,796 --> 00:03:10,330
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

59
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:13,963
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

60
00:03:14,013 --> 00:03:17,572
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

61
00:03:17,622 --> 00:03:21,360
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaah...

62
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:24,060
I'm exhausted.

63
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:28,260
I won't lose!

64
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:35,740
No doubt about it! This is heaven!

65
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:57,840
Hey, hey! Where is God?

66
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:01,460
Kankichi Ryotsu has come to complain!

67
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:06,840
Hey! Where are you? Where? Where? Where?

68
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,720
I see, you ran away because
you knew I was coming.

69
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:15,900
Anyway, let's leave proof that I came here.

70
00:04:16,280 --> 00:04:18,426
Scribble, scribble, scribble,

71
00:04:18,476 --> 00:04:20,360
There, that's done.

72
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,740
Ahahahaha!

73
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:23,740
Whose voice is that?

74
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:25,340
It's God.

75
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:28,180
God, it's me! Where the hell are you?

76
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:31,180
I've been right in front
of you this whole time.

77
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:32,400
Here.

78
00:04:37,960 --> 00:04:41,200
See? I am God.

79
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,200
Kokeee!

80
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,460
Kokeee!

81
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:48,100
Wow, when you're this big, you can't
really walk around at ground level.

82
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,480
Looks like you could get
stepped on if you're not careful.

83
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,540
What a nuisance, really.

84
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:54,300
I don't want to hear that
from the likes of you!

85
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,700
Gods are omniscient and omnipotent.

86
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:58,400
There's no such thing as carelessness.

87
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,960
That's why I know what you're trying to say.

88
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:05,360
That's because you've exceeded 20,000 misdeed points,
you see.

89
00:05:06,140 --> 00:05:08,740
What's this "misdeed points" thing?

90
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:14,340
Every bad human action
has points assigned to it.

91
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:16,880
Telling a lie is 1 point.

92
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:19,960
Peeing in public is 10 points, and so on.

93
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:24,140
Once your total passes 10,000 points,
you're sent to hell after death.

94
00:05:24,140 --> 00:05:27,640
And once you pass 20,000 points,

95
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:29,440
5 points

96
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:33,020
you're turned into a chicken.
That's the rule.

97
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:35,140
I've never done any such wicked things!

98
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,160
Naive, naive.

99
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:40,860
It's all written properly in God's notebook.

100
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:42,900
You think I'd leave it up to you?

101
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:48,280
As a baby, you snatched the
bottle from the baby next to you.

102
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:51,620
That's 12 points to start.

103
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:55,200
In elementary school,
you were a habitual skirt-lifter.

104
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:57,240
That brings it to 122 points.

105
00:05:57,240 --> 00:06:02,740
In middle school, you pranked the principal's bronze statue,
bringing it to 222 points.

106
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,020
Oh dear.

107
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:08,580
And even after becoming a police officer,
you kept showing up late.

108
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:11,680
As for skipping work, it's countless.

109
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:26,820
And yesterday you stole and ate
the taiyaki Chief Ohara bought.

110
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:32,260
That gave you the maximum sin points.

111
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,600
Hold on a second!

112
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:49,160
I added it up, and it's not 20,000 points!

113
00:06:50,900 --> 00:06:52,000
No mistake about it.

114
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,640
It's 19,995 points.

115
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:57,280
What? I calculated it twice!

116
00:06:58,980 --> 00:07:02,700
You claim to be omniscient and omnipotent,
yet you can't even do addition?

117
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,900
Are you an idiot?

118
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:10,380
Well, by rule, the ones place gets rounded!

119
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:12,760
How dare you hurl insults at a human being!

120
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:14,180
This sin is grave!

121
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:16,980
I'm adding 35,000 sin points!

122
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:46,940
*Thunk!*

123
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:50,180
The phone number is...

124
00:07:54,780 --> 00:07:58,400
He's on the phone!
Change me back to my original form!

125
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,580
Change me back! Change me back!
Change me back! Change me back!

126
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,420
Shut up! Hurry up!

127
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:13,220
Change me back!
Change me back! Change me back!

128
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,540
Honestly...

129
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,640
Change me back,
change me back, change me back!

130
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,380
Grr, shut up!

131
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:25,160
Change me back,
change me back, change me back!

132
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,740
Argh, you...

133
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,920
Change me back!
Change me back! Change me back!

134
00:08:35,880 --> 00:08:37,420
Stop it!

135
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:41,980
Stop it!

136
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:48,240
I'm back to human!

137
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:53,420
What are you doing?

138
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:54,620
Let me go!

139
00:08:54,860 --> 00:08:58,940
Someone who fears not even God
like you will run straight to hell!

140
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:05,800
That guy...

141
00:09:05,850 --> 00:09:12,260
God, that is.

142
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:15,420
What if he suddenly tosses me up and I die?

143
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:25,680
What?

144
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:29,560
That guy's a living human, Your Majesty!

145
00:09:30,260 --> 00:09:30,720
What?

146
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:37,040
They sent him to hell
while he's still alive?

147
00:09:37,040 --> 00:09:40,320
That guy must be a real scoundrel.

148
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:44,580
It's been ages since someone
worth tormenting came along!

149
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,360
Who are you?

150
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:48,880
I am the ruler of hell.

151
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,780
King Emma.

152
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,040
The agony of hell.

153
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:56,900
I'll make you taste it to the fullest,
Nyun-nyun.

154
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:16,100
Today I've got a fun date with Megane-chan.

155
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:21,460
Now, which outfit should I wear?

156
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:24,500
What?

157
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:31,400
God, it's serious!

158
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:33,040
What on earth is going on?

159
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:35,860
The legions of hell have invaded Heaven!

160
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:37,300
What?

161
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:37,920
What!?

162
00:10:48,871 --> 00:10:53,820
but Emma, King of Hell,
is not foolish enough to defy me.

163
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,439
Well, the thing is, a revolution
broke out in hell the other day,

164
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:58,580
and apparently they've got a new leader.

165
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:03,640
Emma, King of Hell!

166
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:06,840
Ugh, aaaah, that guy...

167
00:11:10,220 --> 00:11:14,600
Fire! Fire! Fire!

168
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,300
Alright! Fire, fire, fire, shoot them all!

169
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,680
We'll show God the power of hell!

170
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:34,860
To challenge God to a fight...

171
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:38,860
when he's not an opponent
we could ever beat.

172
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:39,400
Hey!

173
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,920
What are you doing?

174
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:43,740
Huh?

175
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:46,980
If you've got time to fiddle with your pockets,
get to work right now!

176
00:11:47,160 --> 00:11:47,840
Yes, sir!

177
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,980
Slash, slash, slash, slash!

178
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:52,820
The Uchiumi and Takaokasha districts
are on the verge of collapse.

179
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:55,400
Already, half of Heaven is a sea of fire.

180
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:05,140
You know-it-all God!

181
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:10,120
Foolish human,
you'll learn the power of God!

182
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:13,680
Dogo, dodan, bajichi, and kaze...
seniority-based promotion and lifetime employment.

183
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:19,420
Underground, chaos, ...human rights issues,
traffic safety, grilled meat set meal.

184
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:42,640
Who goes there?

185
00:12:58,740 --> 00:13:01,620
Calling yourself God, you bastard!

186
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:06,160
For a mere human, you survived
that attack pretty well, didn't you?

187
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:11,520
Don't think this is over, God!

188
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:23,440
You live in a pretty nice place, don't you?

189
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:33,320
What a nice smell.

190
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,840
I found something good!

191
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,020
Itadakimasu!

192
00:13:56,280 --> 00:14:17,380
Hee hee hee hee...

193
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:25,200
At times like this,
a wig really is handy, isn't it?

194
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:29,240
But this is a secret that no one knows.

195
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,900
If it gets out,
God's authority will crumble.

196
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:36,480
Goddess-chan is going to hate me, isn't she?

197
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,900
I saw it, didn't I?

198
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:42,940
You!

199
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:48,640
I always suspected something was fishy,
a god sporting a perm like that.

200
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:50,280
I'll let everyone touch it.

201
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,880
Stop it!

202
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,500
Everyone in Heaven,

203
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:01,560
God's head is actually

204
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:02,740
Returning to Earth.

205
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:10,800
That was a close one.

206
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:16,720
S-senpai! Where did you come from?

207
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:20,740
So I'm inside the police box!

208
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:23,680
Yay! Yay! We did it!

209
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,280
We were worried about you, Ryo-chan.

210
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:29,600
Seriously,
you didn't come back for a whole week!

211
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:31,080
Heh heh.

212
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:31,525
Hey,

213
00:15:31,575 --> 00:15:35,706
Ryotsu! So that you never turn
into a chicken again after this,

214
00:15:35,756 --> 00:15:37,260
mend your ways!

215
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:39,280
Don't worry, it's fine.

216
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:41,160
What do you mean, it's fine!

217
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:45,920
I'll never turn into a chicken again.

218
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:47,360
Because

219
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:48,880
Because

220
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:52,420
I've got God's weakness in my hands.

221
00:15:52,420 --> 00:15:54,240
God's weakness.

222
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:57,020
Strictly between us.

223
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,040
Actually, God's hair is...

224
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:03,700
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no!

225
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:06,240
S-senpai!

226
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,260
Ryo-chan!

227
00:16:07,260 --> 00:16:08,880
Don't worry about it.

228
00:16:08,880 --> 00:16:10,820
He's just knocked out.

229
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:13,140
Waaaaaah!

230
00:16:13,690 --> 00:16:15,560
There's no need to be so surprised.

231
00:16:20,500 --> 00:16:22,520
I am God.

232
00:16:22,520 --> 00:16:24,800
You're God?

233
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,560
I've never seen one before.

234
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:30,480
Normally,
he never comes down to the human world.

235
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:31,608
But,

236
00:16:31,658 --> 00:16:36,760
if this man is left alone, there's no telling
how much trouble he'll cause those around him.

237
00:16:37,380 --> 00:16:41,120
Above all, if he exposes the wig,
it'll be a disaster.

238
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:43,383
Come to think of it, this man

239
00:16:43,433 --> 00:16:47,340
said he had gotten hold of God's weakness.

240
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,460
Move.

241
00:16:48,660 --> 00:16:49,406
Ho ho ho,

242
00:16:49,456 --> 00:16:52,840
"God couldn't possibly have any weakness,"
he said.

243
00:16:53,300 --> 00:16:56,042
No doubt about it. This guy will definitely

244
00:16:56,092 --> 00:16:58,240
expose my secret.

245
00:17:00,160 --> 00:17:02,820
Bad people have to be cut down at the root.

246
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:06,400
We'll pull the root of evil out of this man.

247
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:07,860
Weakling-san

248
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:20,840
How dare you meddle with me like that!

249
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:23,120
I'll make you regret it.

250
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:26,580
Money.

251
00:17:28,240 --> 00:17:29,480
Oh no, what have I done!

252
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,060
I have to do something quickly!

253
00:17:31,140 --> 00:17:32,960
There's no need to panic.

254
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:36,020
Humans have an evil god and a conscience.

255
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:39,460
If we make them fight,
the conscience will always win.

256
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,540
Conscience, come out!

257
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:46,200
Jushii...

258
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:50,080
There's no response at all...

259
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:51,140
Well!

260
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:52,260
Money!

261
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:54,820
Money!

262
00:17:57,140 --> 00:18:00,520
Come out! Conscience! Come out!
Conscience! Come out! Come out!

263
00:18:01,460 --> 00:18:02,020
Nope!

264
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:07,700
Hey! Can't you hear me? Conscience!
Hey! Conscience! Conscience!

265
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:14,300
This man seems to have no conscience.

266
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,100
Nope!

267
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,000
A crab! A crab!

268
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:30,260
Being a lump of desire,
he has tremendous power.

269
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:33,180
If we leave him alone,
things will get terrible.

270
00:18:33,180 --> 00:18:36,620
In that case,
it seems I'll have to stop him myself.

271
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:39,100
Battle preparations!

272
00:18:46,440 --> 00:18:49,760
Come on, I'll take you on!

273
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:52,780
What, he wants to fight

274
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:54,260
Transform!

275
00:19:04,740 --> 00:19:06,000
Killer first strike!

276
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:15,760
Got him!

277
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,720
Left straight!

278
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:26,160
How do you like that? Learned your lesson?

279
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:32,180
You're too naive!

280
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:45,580
They say those who scorn a single
yen end up crying over a single yen.

281
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:47,560
Even small change has to be handled carefully,
you know.

282
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:53,040
Let's cut this out already.

283
00:19:56,460 --> 00:19:58,000
Just as I thought, he really is God.

284
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:59,340
So strong.

285
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,680
How about it?

286
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:06,660
I was wrong. I'm sorry.

287
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:09,640
I'll quit being an evil
spirit and become a conscience.

288
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,380
Is that the truth?

289
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:12,680
Good.

290
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:17,800
Seriously?

291
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:21,160
Believing what a demon says, you fool!

292
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:23,960
After all,
money is everything in this world.

293
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,320
Damn you!

294
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:32,120
Lord, I have a good idea.

295
00:20:36,380 --> 00:20:38,340
Hmm I see.

296
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:39,100
Right.

297
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,080
Hey, demon! Look at that!

298
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:52,040
Isn't that the bell-ringing tree!

299
00:20:56,940 --> 00:20:59,940
With this,
there's no need to worry about the bell!

300
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:23,160
Go on, fly off to the ends of the universe!

301
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,280
Ruined by money, of all things.

302
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:28,960
That's just how he would end up

303
00:21:29,860 --> 00:21:30,900
Ryo-chan

304
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,520
Ryo-chan

305
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:48,520
Could this be...?

306
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,500
Yuko

307
00:21:50,860 --> 00:21:53,180
Excuse me.

308
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:55,140
Aliens

309
00:21:55,140 --> 00:21:57,660
Please take a look at this.

310
00:22:02,040 --> 00:22:04,180
Ryo-chan

311
00:22:04,180 --> 00:22:10,620
Our planet has been
troubled because of this man.

312
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:13,120
Please do something about him.

313
00:22:15,220 --> 00:22:18,400
Even on other planets,
he's causing trouble...

314
00:22:18,900 --> 00:22:21,080
He's a disgrace to Earth, isn't he.

315
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:22,400
Honestly.

316
00:22:22,400 --> 00:22:23,900
Gane da gane

